  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nClearing should continue through this afternoon under building \nhigh pressure. The high is expected to be overhead tonight, with\nclear skies and light wind. Efficient radiational cooling \nshould result in below freezing temperatures for most of the \narea. Nudged guidance toward the colder solutions with these \nfavorable conditions. Along with the cold temperatures, there is\na chance for river valley fog to develop due to the large\ntemperature difference between the air and water ( in the low \n60s).\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\nModel ensembles indicate a closed low should remain off of the\nMid Atlantic/Carolina coast through much of the upcoming week,\nwith a trough along the western CONUS. During this week, a \nridge extending from Central CONUS to the Upper Ohio \nValley/Great Lakes region is forecast to remain relatively \nstationary as it builds in between these two systems. Dry \nweather is expected through this period, with gradually warming \ntemperatures through mid week as 500 mb heights rise. Readings \nby mid to late week should be around 5 degrees above average in\nthe mid to upper 60s.",
